/*!
    \page getting-started.html
    \title Getting Started
    \brief Build Qt DynamicDashboard and embed it in a Qt Quick application.

    \section1 Build Requirements

    * CMake 3.21 or newer.
    * Qt 6.8 or newer for the library.
    * Qt 6.10 or newer to build all current examples.
    * A C++17 compatible compiler.

    \section1 Configure and Build

    Clone the repository:

    \badcode
    git clone https://github.com/mbr1376/DashboardPluginQml.git
    cd DashboardPluginQml
    \endcode

    Set the path to the Qt installation. Adjust the path for your system:

    \badcode
    export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$HOME/Qt/6.10.1/gcc_64"
    \endcode

    Configure and build the project:

    \badcode
    cmake -S . -B build \\
      -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH="$CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH" \\
      -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=ON

    cmake --build build --parallel
    \endcode

    To build only the library, configure with \c BUILD_EXAMPLES set to \c OFF.

    \section1 Use DashboardView

    Import the Dashboard module and place \l DashboardView in the application's
    QML scene:

    \qml
    import QtQuick
    import Dashboard

    Window {
        visible: true
        width: 1400
        height: 900

        DashboardView {
            anchors.fill: parent
        }
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Load Data

    \l DashboardView provides methods for supplying data directly, parsing
    JSON or CSV text, loading a local file, and retrieving JSON from a REST
    endpoint. See \l {data-handling.html}{Data Handling} for details.
*/
